  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;be a natural number and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be the function defined by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mi>if</mi></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is such that the area of the region bounded by the curves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>, then the maximum value of the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is</p>"
  },
